\b Source\b0 
17:15 (king) \u183? 18:15 (prophet) \u183? 18:2 (priest)
Dominant. All authority is given, not arrogated; illegitimate
sources are rejected.
Why permit a king at all if it is so risky?


\b Trajectory\b0 
17:14 (\u8216?when you come into the land\u8217?)
Thin. Points forward to the future, instituted order.
Is the self-exalting king past, or a lasting temptation?


\b Will\b0 
16:20 (pursue) \u183? 16:18 (appoint) \u183? 21:6 (wash hands)
Bounded-active: pursue justice, establish offices, carry
responsibility.
Where does \u8216?pursue\u8217? pass over into \u8216?grasp\u8217??


\b Coherence\b0 
17:20 (heart not lifted) \u183? 18:22 (test) \u183? 19:15,21 (witnesses,
proportionality)
Dominant, interlocks with Source. One system of limits on power;
authority stays testable.
How do you distinguish \u8216?correctable\u8217? from \u8216?open to anything\u8217??



Reactivity: mildly present (\u8216?not like the nations\u8217?, 18:9) but not
foregrounded \u8212? note it as observation, and do not impose it.

\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par

\u8594? Summarize the movement: what does the text unmask, what frame
does it put in its place, what response follows, and capture it in one
core sentence.
\b What is unmasked?\b0  Authority that cuts itself loose
from the source and makes itself the measure \u8212? the king whose heart
lifts itself (17:20), the presumptuous prophet (18:20), the false
witness (19:18).
\b What frame does the text put in its place?\b0  Authority
that is given and therefore lets itself be tested: under the Torah, with
witnesses, proportional, accountable \u8212? as a brother among brothers.
\b What concrete response and formation follow?\b0  Pursue
justice by righteous means; receive your place and stay under it; carry
responsibility, even for blood that does not cling to your hands.
\b Core sentence:\b0  Pursuing justice: authority that
is given, and precisely therefore bounded and accountable.
Horizon (not this week\u8217?s theme, but the ground): beneath all this
lies the one question \u8212? received or grasped. Self-arrogated authority is
the grasped form; received, testable authority the received form. This
time the text pressed hardest on the Source\u8211?Coherence relation.

